practice_explanation = "Linear Search shines when the array is small (under 50 items) or when the data is unsorted. For tiny lists, the overhead of a smarter algorithm isn't worth it. For unsorted data, Binary Search simply won't work. For LARGE SORTED data, use Binary Search instead — it's much faster."
